{%- comment -%}
  Google Customer Reviews — Survey Opt-In
  CBD Surgeons & Surgeons, LLC / surgeonsolution.io
  Merchant ID: 5586792336

  DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS:
  ========================
  This script runs on the ORDER CONFIRMATION PAGE (thank you page).
  Shopify does NOT allow theme files on the checkout/order-status page
  unless you are on Shopify Plus with checkout.liquid.

  TO INSTALL:
  1. Go to Shopify Admin → Settings → Checkout
  2. Scroll to "Order status page" → "Additional scripts"
  3. Paste the EXACT content between the ═══ markers below
  4. Save

  The Liquid variables (checkout.order_number, checkout.email, etc.)
  are only available in the order status page context.

  WHAT IT DOES:
  - After checkout, Google shows the customer an opt-in to receive
    a review survey via email
  - Reviews feed into Google Merchant Center and can show as
    seller ratings in Google Shopping and Search ads
  - Directly improves ad CTR and product listing trust

  SEO IMPACT:
  - Seller ratings in Google Shopping ads (star ratings)
  - Google Merchant Center trust signals
  - Increased CTR on Shopping and Search campaigns

  BUD IMPACT:
  - None. This script only runs on the Shopify-hosted checkout page,
    which is outside the theme's DOM and BUD's scope.

  LAST UPDATED: 2026-01-27
  OPERATOR: Ryan Bolda, 130 Dickinson St, Mount Clemens, MI 48043
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  COPY EVERYTHING BELOW THIS LINE INTO:
  Shopify Admin → Settings → Checkout → Order status page → Additional scripts
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

<!-- Google Customer Reviews — CBD Surgeons (Merchant ID: 5586792336) -->
<script src="https://apis.google.com/js/platform.js?onload=renderOptIn" async defer></script>

<script>
  window.renderOptIn = function() {
    window.gapi.load('surveyoptin', function() {
      window.gapi.surveyoptin.render({
        "merchant_id": 5586792336,
        "order_id": "{{ checkout.order_number }}",
        "email": "{{ checkout.email }}",
        "delivery_country": "{{ checkout.shipping_address.country_code }}",
        "estimated_delivery_date": "{{ checkout.created_at | date: '%s' | plus: 604800 | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}",
        "products": [
          {%- for line_item in checkout.line_items -%}
            {%- if line_item.variant.barcode != blank -%}
              {"gtin": "{{ line_item.variant.barcode }}"}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      });
    });
  }
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  STOP COPYING HERE
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  NOTES:
  - checkout.order_number → Shopify order number (e.g. #1042)
  - checkout.email → customer email from checkout
  - checkout.shipping_address.country_code → ISO country code (e.g. "US")
  - estimated_delivery_date → order date + 7 days (1-2 handling + 2-5 transit)
  - products[].gtin → product barcodes from Shopify variant data
    (only included if barcode is populated in Shopify Admin)

  TO ADD BARCODES:
  Shopify Admin → Products → [Product] → Variants → edit variant → Barcode (ISBN, UPC, GTIN)
  This feeds both the Product schema (theme.liquid) and Google Customer Reviews.

  OPTIONAL: STOREFRONT BADGE
  If you want the Google Customer Reviews badge on your storefront,
  add this to theme.liquid before </body>:

    <script src="https://apis.google.com/js/platform.js?onload=renderBadge" async defer></script>
    <script>
      window.renderBadge = function() {
        var r498498498 = document.createElement("div");
        r498498498.id = "___ratingbadge";
        document.body.appendChild(r498498498);
        window.gapi.load("ratingbadge", function() {
          window.gapi.ratingbadge.render(r498498498, {"merchant_id": 5586792336, "position": "BOTTOM_RIGHT"});
        });
      }
    </script>

  If adding the badge, ensure apis.google.com is in the CSP (already added in theme.liquid).
{%- endcomment -%}
